# Agent Memory Techniques — vendored curated subset

The notebooks in this directory are from **Nir Diamant, "Agent Memory Techniques"**
(https://github.com/NirDiamant/Agent_Memory_Techniques), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

Curated for the KDD'26 tutorial Phase 1 (hands-on):
- `conversation_buffer_memory.ipynb` — technique 01 (Short-term)
- `vector_store_memory.ipynb` — technique 06 (Long-term)
- `episodic_memory.ipynb` — technique 09 (Long-term)
- `semantic_memory.ipynb` — technique 10 (Long-term)
- `hierarchical_memory_layers.ipynb` — technique 13 (Cognitive)
- `memory_retrieval_patterns.ipynb` — technique 20 (Retrieval)

`utils/helpers.py` is the upstream shared helper module these notebooks import. The remaining 24
techniques are surveyed (with links) in `phase1_agent_memory_techniques.ipynb`; open the upstream
repository for the full set.

## Running these notebooks (Phase 1)
They need an LLM. Point them at the free OpenAI-compatible **OpenAI-compatible endpoint** by exporting, before
launching Jupyter:

```bash
export OPENAI_API_KEY=-<your-key>
export OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
```

(`get_openai_client()` in `utils/helpers.py` calls `OpenAI(api_key=key)`, which honours
`OPENAI_BASE_URL`, so the notebooks transparently use the gateway.) Install dependencies with the
upstream `requirements.txt`; technique 06 additionally needs `chromadb`.

Apache-2.0 attribution is retained; see `../../../licenses/APACHE-2.0.txt` and the upstream
`CITATION.cff`.
